verification
    V1  One boundary, hard deletion and fail-closed inputs
        Establishes @O1 and @O2. Keep one package boundary.
        Retain package/import/ESM and Effect/React peer boundaries with the accepted
        replacement. No package, contract, runtime or declaration combines old and
        replacement vocabularies.

        For every DELETE/REPLACE value or shape, prove runtime export absence.
        Prove absence from active declarations and imports. Reject unsupported forms
        before actor creation, memory mutation, operation acquisition, events,
        external work or evidence. A deleted name may appear only in this ledger,
        the non-normative deferred record, historical provenance or a negative proof.
        Add no alias, overload, adapter, parser branch or wrapper that translates it.

        Retain environmental boundaries while removing old capability shapes.
        Deleted inputs fail before side effects, and deleted-only implementation
        paths leave the active package. @V5 owns runtime absence, declaration
        negatives and fail-closed behavior. @V6 owns retained boundaries and
        cleanup. Receipts remain pending under @plan.Verification.V7.
    V2  Explicit writes, synchronous commands, Stories and artifacts
        Establishes @O1. Operation results never write canonical resource data
        implicitly. Only explicit setData mappings on accepted transaction/stream
        surfaces are authoritative and generation-safe (@plan.Verification.V3).
        Public actor.send(event) remains synchronous void over the production
        mailbox. Story acknowledgement stays package-private over that mailbox.
        Add no public Promise overload or second actor engine
        (@plan.Verification.V2, @plan.Verification.V4, @plan.Verification.V7, @O2).

        Stories use exactly these builders:
        - `story.app(runtimeSetup, options?)`
        - `story.machine(machine, options?)`
        - `story.actor(machine, options?)`
        Accept only defined command and evidence forms. Reject old Story names,
        aliases, parallel harnesses and injection commands.

        Server, Persistence, artifact, inspect and CLI models use accepted app,
        actor, compound-state, context, lifecycle and operation identities. Retain
        codecs, bounds, sinks and formatting only when they preserve no deleted
        surface. Follow @plan.Verification.V6 for artifact migration. Reject legacy
        root, child, final, replay and mutable-harness/Story forms at the wire
        boundary. Invent no commands, schemas, migration algorithms or old identities.

        Stories and evidence are owned by
        @plan.Verification.V4; artifact/CLI and final gate references are
        in @plan.Verification.V6 and @plan.Verification.V7.
        CONTRACT.md §8 examples and proposed surfaces do not change this active
        contract.
    V3  Disposition and retained-boundary ledger
        Establishes @O2 and @O3. Before cutover, check each row against owning Plan
        requirements, source traces, code, declarations, docs, consumers, Stories, fixtures, tests,
        tasks, registries and proofs. The complete current disposition ledger is:

        **Views and actor identities**
        - **DELETE (DEL-001):** Registered Flow views, exported View/IDs, module.views,
          registered lookup, useView(view), view-bound can. @plan.Verification.V5
          retains only passive useView(actor, selector).
        - **DELETE (DEL-002):** Child constructor/descriptors/inputs/IDs/lifecycle/
          completion/snapshots/addressing/persistence/Story/model; recursive
          substates in one actor and explicit actors for independent workflows remain.
        - **DELETE (DEL-003):** dynamicMachines, RootActor/DynamicActor, automatic roots,
          runtime.actor(machine), ID-bearing local creation and dynamic-root
          persistence. Retain named module records, closed App.M and explicit identities.

        **Ownership, grammar and operations**
        - **REPLACE (DEL-004):** active|disposed, handle disposal, DynamicActor.dispose,
          auto-root ownership/category identity; explicit owner leases and prepared|
          active|suspended|disposed remain.
        - **REPLACE (DEL-005):** root initial, flat-only grammar, final kind/onDone/output,
          completion mailbox shutdown, Boolean reentry and conflicting recursive
          handlers. Retain recursive states/default/exact reentry/ordinary
          terminal-looking leaves/transition actions. Remove the old ban on actions.
        - **DELETE (DEL-006):** Generic activity kit/methods, public refs/byKey/byLane,
          bound entries, generic resource/transaction get and enumeration. Retain
          named O families and P/K/key/getState/getData.

        **React, Stories and artifacts**
        - **REPLACE (DEL-007):** Recursive structural sharing, custom equality/comparator
          hooks; one scalar/non-record and named-record Object.is contract remains.
        - **REPLACE (DEL-008):** React-created shells/swapping, root-only useActor,
          useResource, broad subscriptions, per-actor Context, binding components,
          view-object hooks; FlowProvider and production-owned useActor/useActorByRef
          remain.
        - **REPLACE (DEL-009):** Callable story, with, bare apps/live Runtime inputs,
          perform/deliver/receive/simulate/flush/settle/setTime/final/replay,
          mutable harnesses and old runners. The accepted replacements are the builders,
          complete Implementations, process/advanceTo/checkpoint.actor and run.end at
          @plan.Verification.V4.
        - **REPLACE (DEL-010):** Mutable v1 boot/hydration, fabricated root/child/final
          fields, replay inspection, duplicate formatters, arbitrary scenario commands,
          old Story artifact schemas. Retain codecs/bounds/sinks/CLI formatters and
          update proof discipline to accepted identities.

        **Historical sources**
        - **HISTORICAL (DEL-011, physical cleanup pending):** Old implementation/contracts
          pack, obsolete compatibility matrix and phase/task docs prescribing deleted
          surfaces. Source status now records provenance; Workflow Plans own mapped
          semantics. Remove these files only after mapped proofs and the final no-residue
          audit. Git history is the archive.

        **Retained environmental and runtime boundaries**
        - **RETAIN (RET-001):** Package routes, ESM/import conditions, Effect peer identity
          and supported React peer compatibility.
        - **RETAIN (RET-002):** Synchronous actor.send(event):void, production mailbox,
          Runtime-scoped stores, generation fencing, Cause classification and cleanup
          ordering. Remove fields encoding deleted roots/children/final/Story forms.
        - **RETAIN (RET-003):** Resource and transaction status discriminants.
        - **RETAIN (RET-004):** Canonical key/getState/getData, transition actions and
          accepted O/P/K identity.
        - **RETAIN (RET-005):** FlowProvider, revised useActor/useActorByRef and passive
          selector observation.

        These dispositions are normative targets, not evidence they are implemented.
        This ledger belongs to @O2 and @V3. Runtime export, declaration, retained-
        boundary and cleanup checks belong to @V5 and @V6. Final no-residue
        receipts belong to @plan.Verification.V7.
    V4  No-residue audit
        Establishes @O2 and @O3. For every DELETE/REPLACE row, verify all six:
        1. Owning Plan requirements, source traces, consumers, Stories, fixtures,
           tests and task files use accepted or explicitly retained surfaces only.
        2. Runtime export tests show deleted values and namespaces are absent.
        3. Declaration tests reject deleted types, overloads, properties, deep imports
           and authoring shapes.
        4. Deleted inputs fail before actor, memory, operation, event, external-work
           or evidence side effects.
        5. No alias, adapter, registry, translator, parser branch or deletion-only
           implementation remains.
        6. Live consumers exercise accepted replacements through production owners.
        Source scans support audits but never replace runtime or declaration proofs.

        The old contract name may appear only in a negative absence test, not
        positive usage, supported overload, active glossary, compatibility
        recommendation or replacement recipe. The ledger does not remove RET rows.
        Reference consumers rewrite deleted calls. Selector files may move and
        unused fixtures may be removed/promoted; layout itself is not a deletion
        rule. One complete mapped audit runs before @O2 removal/classification;
        do not duplicate the full historical absence matrix in ordinary tasks.

        Check: one final no-consumer/deletion audit plus owner proofs; filenames and
        token scans are supporting evidence only. Exact audit/task path is pending.
        Cutover-specific detail is this Plan; central proof receipt is
        @plan.Verification.V7.
    V5  Runtime exports, declarations and behavior
        Establishes @O1 and @O2. Verify every DELETE/REPLACE row in @V3 through
        package entrypoints and retained owners.

        - Prove deleted runtime exports and namespaces are absent, including deep
          imports and file registries. Retained surfaces remain available.
        - Reject deleted values, types, overloads, properties, imports, authoring
          forms and Story forms in packed declarations and public consumers.
        - Submit deleted inputs and prove failure before side effects.
        - Prove accepted replacements through production owners.
        - Reject compatibility aliases, adapters, parser branches and parallel
          runtime, actor, Story, operation or selector implementations.

        Pass requires runtime absence, declaration negatives and behavioral
        side-effect rejection. Source scans alone do not pass. Named test paths
        and receipts remain pending. Production proof owners are @plan.Verification.V1,
        @plan.Verification.V2 and @plan.Verification.V7.
    V6  Retained compatibility, cleanup and surviving authority
        Establishes @O1 and @O3. Verify every RETAIN row in @V3 remains without
        deleted names.

        - Check package imports and Effect/React peer boundaries.
        - Check the synchronous mailbox, production ownership and status
          discriminants for resources and transactions.
        - Check canonical identity, operations, actions, FlowProvider, revised
          actor hooks and passive views through accepted production owners.
        - Remove or mark historical tests devoted only to deleted behavior after
          replacement proofs pass. Replace token-only tests with behavior proofs.
        - Map each live old obligation to an owning Plan or proof before source cleanup.
          Keep Git history as the archive.

        Require one current Plan owner for every live obligation. Do not lose transferred
        requirements. This Plan does not claim implementation. Check the mapping,
        @plan.Verification.V7, packed consumers, package/browser gates and broad
        workspace gates. Physical source cleanup and product cutover remain pending under Q1.
    V7  Final coordinated cutover
        Establishes @O1 and @O3. Apply all target outcomes only after each mapped
        implementation proof, retained-boundary check, no-residue audit, final
        proving application and package gate is recorded. Required integration
        gates are the shared sequence in @plan.Verification.V7. This Plan adds
        @V5, @V6 and the @O2 disposition rather than a duplicate proof matrix.

        Historical behavior entries are provenance, not an input to compatibility
        choices. No historical entry is an open compatibility blocker. Workflow Tasks
        own current implementation obligations; Beads records and old proof receipts
        are historical evidence. CONTRACT.md §11
        is an unaccepted proposal checklist, not a proof receipt. Keep every checkbox
        unchecked until its executable proof and focused or broad gates run.
        Source review, typechecking, generated output or diff check alone does not
        close it. Proposal areas map to @plan.Verification.V1 through
        @plan.Verification.V7. No checkbox, proof or gate is marked complete here.

        Check @plan.Verification.V1 through @plan.Verification.V8 and this Plan's
        @V1 through @V6. Also run package, packed-consumer, browser and final
        workspace gates. Keep every receipt pending until the check runs. Make no
        package-promotion claim before then.

questions
    Q1  Product cutover after authority transfer
        Workflow Plans now own migrated semantics. The source pack records this
        transfer and remains provenance until the no-residue audit passes; source
        cleanup is a separate gate. Product documentation keeps its owner; Workflow
        Tasks own current status, while Beads records remain historical snapshots.
        Package promotion and product cutover remain pending under
        @O3 and @V7; this Plan records no implementation or gate completion.

